 "summary_html": "<p>In typography and word processing, a <b>page header</b> is text that is separated from the body text and appears at the top of a printed page. Word-processing programs usually allow for the configuration of page headers, which are typically identical throughout a work except in aspects such as page numbers. \n[\nThe counterpart at the bottom of the page is called a page footer ; its content is typically similar and often complementary to that of the page header.</p>",
